1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:13,013
[intense music playing]

2
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:24,566
That brooch. Is that Perry's?

3
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:26,109
How's it going with them?

4
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:27,861
Can we talk about your love life?

5
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:31,156
That sad bun reeks of boy problems.

6
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:32,365
Is this about Cam?

7
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,034
No, it's not him.

8
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:35,493
There's someone else?

9
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:37,662
I hooked up with Josh.

10
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:39,205
[laughing]

11
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,373
[both laughing]

12
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:44,753
-Wow. I cannot leave you unsupervised.
-No need to worry about that.

13
00:00:44,836 --> 00:00:51,051
He's firmly in the past tense,
and I'm focusing on me and my rowing now.

14
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:57,932
-[intense music continues]
-[heavy breathing]

15
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:01,644
I was previously prescribed beta-blockers

16
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:04,647
for hypertrophic
obstructive cardiomyopathy,

17
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:07,567
but it's not enough
to keep up with my rowing.

18
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:10,987
You have HOCM.
And you want to keep rowing?

19
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:13,198
You understand
there's serious risks to that.

20
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:17,327
That's why I came here.
I heard you take specialized cases.

21
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:19,788
I will make it worth your while.

22
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:22,874
I never saw this report.

23
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:24,000
Mm-hmm.

24
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:30,090
And I never gave you
this medication, disopyramide.

25
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:33,009
It'll mitigate the risks
in the short term.

26
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:34,552
How do I get a refill?

27
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:38,014
You don't. It's a temporary fix.

28
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:40,767
It's only a matter of time
before it stops working.

29
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:46,314
[grunts]

30
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:55,907
Hey, Dad.

31
00:01:56,407 --> 00:02:00,537
You know, I finished those oil changes.
Cool if I clock out, get some training in?

32
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:03,206
Sorry, bud, I still need you.
We're really behind,

33
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:05,583
and it's just you and me
for the next little while.

34
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:07,418
Okay.

35
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:09,462
I'll get my tools.

36
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,048
[sighs heavily]

37
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:24,769
[Britney] This is sad.

38
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:29,023
Like you don't hide a stash of Skittles
in your Pilates mat.

39
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:32,610
-[Baloo laughs]
-Yeah, yeah.

40
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:38,408
Being single is humiliating.

41
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:39,450
Humiliating?

42
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:44,122
Logan used me to sabotage the team,
and I fell for it.

43
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:46,583
This is the last day
we drown our feelings in snacks.

44
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:49,961
-No promises.
-Bronson, this is beneath us.

45
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,880
Binging on carbs is a cliché.

46
00:02:57,677 --> 00:02:58,887
When did this happen?

47
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:00,805
What? Like it's hard?

48
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:02,724
I know you got hurt.

49
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:06,436
But the best way to get over a guy
is to crush them

50
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:08,563
and take everything they love
for yourself.

51
00:03:18,781 --> 00:03:19,657
[machine beeping]

52
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,451
[trainer] Stay in the zone, Ryder.

53
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:23,536
This is how you wanted
to spend your weekend.

54
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,080
I didn't get to the Olympics
giving 95 percent.

55
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:28,082
-Who's got 100?
-Me.

56
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:30,293
You're slowing down. Who's got 100?

57
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:31,377
Me!

58
00:03:34,214 --> 00:03:36,132
[Hayden] All right, crew. That's enough.

59
00:03:43,514 --> 00:03:46,309
Glad you took my suggestion
to get a 2K in this morning.

60
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:49,229
The Norfolk Indoor Rowing Invitational
is coming up.

61
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:53,107
And only those
with strong erg scores qualify.

62
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:54,943
Now this year, as a bonus,

63
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:58,446
there will be a scout
for the junior national team.

64
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:02,075
And guess what? Cam, Josh,

65
00:04:02,158 --> 00:04:04,202
Ryder, and Baloo.

66
00:04:04,702 --> 00:04:05,620
You've made the cut.

67
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:07,080
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

68
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,831
Let's go!

69
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:12,502
And on the girls' side, Teagan, you're up.

70
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:15,463
-No way!
-[Baloo] Nice, Tea!

71
00:04:15,546 --> 00:04:18,091
-Time to show us what you can do.
-[Teagan laughs]

72
00:04:19,175 --> 00:04:24,722
[rousing music playing]

73
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:30,144
{\an8}You got a PR. Not bad.

74
00:04:30,645 --> 00:04:33,523
{\an8}-Looks like Cam's my only competition.
-[scoffs]

75
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:36,943
{\an8}Well, enjoy this moment.
It's not gonna last.

76
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:41,948
{\an8}Okay, everyone,
make sure to fill out your sign-up sheets.

77
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:45,702
This is an individual competition,
but we're still rooting for you all.

78
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:55,295
Can you pass the clipboard?

79
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:05,305
Saw you on the erg.
You're looking pretty good.

80
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:06,389
Yup.

81
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,851
Yeah, I guess I deserve that.

82
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,229
How long am I gonna get the cold shoulder?

83
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:16,399
Life is long.

84
00:05:16,482 --> 00:05:18,484
[sassy EDM playing]

85
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:24,991
-[Baloo] Can I ask you something?
-Yeah, sure.

86
00:05:25,074 --> 00:05:26,367
I saw the competition list.

87
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:29,829
Logan's gonna be there.
And I wanna kick his ass.

88
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:34,834
I love the fire. Okay?
But he's really good. Westvale's best.

89
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:36,711
I know. But…

90
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:39,380
I'm the hurt party, right?
So I deserve to beat him.

91
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,466
Well, I'm not sure about that logic.

92
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:45,720
Come on, you've been watching me, right?
What do I need to do?

93
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:49,974
He's got you flustered.
When you're flustered, you're messy.

94
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:53,019
If you come in hot,
you're going to burn out.

95
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:54,896
Don't let him get to you.

96
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:58,816
Okay. Okay, okay.
Yeah, I think I can do that.

97
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:01,194
-Yeah, you got it.
-Thanks, man.

98
00:06:01,277 --> 00:06:02,278
Yeah.

99
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:15,833
-Hey, Mom.
-Hey.

100
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:18,586
I've got news.

101
00:06:19,337 --> 00:06:21,589
-Mm?
-I'm invited to the Norfolk Invitational.

102
00:06:21,672 --> 00:06:22,673
[gasps]

103
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:25,760
Amazing. Yes! [laughs]

104
00:06:25,843 --> 00:06:27,345
-[phone buzzing]
-Oh!

105
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:28,930
[gasps] Hold on.

106
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:35,520
Richard, I got the flowers you sent
for my promotion.

107
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,063
You didn't have to.

108
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:40,358
Well, you kind of did, didn't you?

109
00:06:40,441 --> 00:06:44,695
[Richard] <i>President of Luxury Travel.</i>
<i>Congratulations.</i>

110
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:49,200
<i>I wanted the job,</i>
<i>but I'm actually glad that you got it.</i>

111
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:52,662
<i>You see,</i>
<i>everyone wants in on luxury travel,</i>

112
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:54,455
<i>including the other airlines,</i>

113
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:57,667
<i>so I convinced Dad to sell</i>
<i>you and the division off to the Dutch.</i>

114
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:58,626
What?

115
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:01,045
<i>Don't worry. You'll still have</i>
<i>a beautiful corner office</i>

116
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:02,630
<i>-in Rotterdam.</i>
-[sinister music playing]

117
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:04,257
You snake.

118
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:06,092
<i>Enjoy the windmills.</i>

119
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:07,844
[gasps]

120
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:08,970
[phone clatters]

121
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:09,929
[exclaims]

122
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,681
[suppressed scream]

123
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:15,476
-Mom.
-He outplayed us.

124
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:18,020
We're on the outside now.

125
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,730
It's not fair.

126
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:24,485
Regis Airlines belong to us
as much as them.

127
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:29,323
Yeah, well, it'll be impossible
to get back on Viktor's radar now.

128
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:41,127
There's one thing
that Granddad can't ignore.

129
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:44,547
It's always burned him
that he never made it to the Olympics.

130
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:48,009
But I've got a shot.

131
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:53,264
The junior national team scout
is gonna be at the Norfolk Invitationals.

132
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:56,934
You'd be on track
to being the first Regis at the Olympics.

133
00:07:57,018 --> 00:07:58,436
If I win.

134
00:07:59,228 --> 00:08:01,564
Do whatever it takes.

135
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,945
[engine starting]

136
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:20,875
So this is where you live.

137
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:24,086
What do you want, Ryder?

138
00:08:24,795 --> 00:08:26,964
You know, tomorrow's race
is down to me and you.

139
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:28,799
Pretty sure it's just me.

140
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:33,429
I've noticed you picking up extra shifts
here at the shop.

141
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,182
You help me, and I'll help you.

142
00:08:36,265 --> 00:08:37,725
[uneasy music playing]

143
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:41,812
I need the scout looking at me tomorrow.

144
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:46,567
So… what's it going to take
for you to make that happen?

145
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,278
Are you asking me to throw the race?

146
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:53,950
I'm asking you… to name your price.

147
00:08:55,409 --> 00:08:56,661
What do you want?

148
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:00,331
An erg? A vacation?

149
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:02,792
A car?

150
00:09:05,294 --> 00:09:06,462
I can go higher.

151
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:07,964
Get out.

152
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:10,675
Everyone has a price, Dillinger.

153
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:22,562
[upbeat music playing]

154
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:25,314
[Ella and Hayden laughing]

155
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:28,025
Teagan?

156
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:31,028
Teagan.

157
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:33,948
-The coast is clear.
-Okay.

158
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:36,617
-I will see you later tonight. Okay?
-Okay.

159
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:38,869
I gotta get in the shower.

160
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:40,329
Wish I could join you.

161
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:42,623
[door opening]

162
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,377
-[Hayden] Oh! Uh…
-[Teagan screams]

163
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:48,421
-Oh my God! Coach Hayden…
-Teagan.

164
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:50,631
Why are you here?

165
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:53,467
-I-I-I can explain.
-With your shirt open.

166
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:55,386
Probably a conversation
for you and your mom.

167
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:58,848
Did you stay over with me in the house?

168
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:00,141
I should go.

169
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:02,184
Oh, this is so not cool!

170
00:10:02,268 --> 00:10:03,394
See you at practice.

171
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:05,688
Mom!

172
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:08,399
-[groans] Oh my God!
-[door opens and closes]

173
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:12,862
[Cam's dad] Don't say there's nothing
you can do. You can give me more time.

174
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:14,989
I can get the 48K.

175
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:17,199
I heard you the first time.

176
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:19,535
Jackasses.

177
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:20,995
What's going on, Dad?

178
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:23,247
Oh, nothing you need to worry about, son.

179
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:26,042
$48,000 is a lot of money.

180
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,419
-Are we going to be okay?
-Look.

181
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:31,589
Whatever happens with the bank,
we're gonna be okay.

182
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:34,008
So just get out there,

183
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:36,636
and you show that scout
what you're made of.

184
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,180
-Okay?
-Mm-hmm, all right.

185
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:42,933
Knock 'em dead.

186
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:53,235
Rowers are divided
by age, schools, and rank.

187
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:55,988
All you gotta do is give them
their erg numbers and start times.

188
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,365
Then check them off here.

189
00:10:57,448 --> 00:11:00,493
Explain again why I'm giving up
my Saturday to play attendance cop?

190
00:11:00,576 --> 00:11:03,454
Because last Saturday, I went to
no less than six record stores with you.

191
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:06,040
And I saved you from the other four.
You're welcome.

192
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:08,876
-Thank you.
-[Teagan clears throat]

193
00:11:08,959 --> 00:11:11,212
-Nice to see you again. Love the shirt.
-Love it.

194
00:11:11,295 --> 00:11:13,673
And how it is completely on.

195
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:17,385
I'm gonna check with the refs.
I will see you inside.

196
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:21,055
Sorry, we ever formally met?

197
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:24,725
I'm Teagan. Our parents are dating.

198
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:28,396
-I'm Madison. And I already knew that.
-Wait, how long have you known?

199
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:30,356
It's been a few weeks.

200
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:31,899
Weeks?

201
00:11:31,982 --> 00:11:34,652
So you're in race 2 on erg 14.

202
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:38,447
Oh, my… Weeks? What the hell?
Why didn't they just tell me?

203
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:40,741
I mean, in their defense, your reaction.

204
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,618
Come on, it is perfectly appropriate.

205
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:45,079
-I saw your dad's abs.
-Hey! Too far.

206
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:46,038
Exactly.

207
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:47,957
I'm not your enemy.

208
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:52,211
Some advice? There are five stages
to parents dating again.

209
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:54,213
Anger, denial.

210
00:11:54,714 --> 00:12:00,344
Anger again. Then, "You're not my mom,"
and… finally, begrudging acceptance.

211
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:03,889
-[Cam] Madison.
-We locked in?

212
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:06,475
Running up stairs, eating raw eggs,
punching meat in the freezer?

213
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,644
No more <i>Rocky </i>marathons for you.

214
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:10,563
You're in race 1 at erg 10.

215
00:12:12,022 --> 00:12:13,232
You got this, Dillinger.

216
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,028
Good luck out there.

217
00:12:18,529 --> 00:12:19,530
Thank you.

218
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:27,663
-He's so different with you.
-Dillinger? Boy's same as ever.

219
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:30,166
How long have you guys been friends?

220
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:32,168
I've known him since his bowl-cut phase.

221
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:33,586
Ah. [laughs]

222
00:12:33,669 --> 00:12:36,547
Yeah, he and I… used to be friends, but…

223
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:38,966
Barely talks to me now.

224
00:12:40,634 --> 00:12:41,552
How can I fix it?

225
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:45,973
Look, he's going through his own thing.
It's him. He just needs some time.

226
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:49,351
Yeah.

227
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:52,229
Thanks.

228
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:56,567
Bronson Garner.

229
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:58,486
Thanks.

230
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,448
[clears throat] So you do exist.

231
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,159
Just here to race and take gold.

232
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:07,536
Good luck with that.
I know how easily you give up.

233
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,040
At least I don't cheat to win.

234
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:20,257
Ryder Regis.

235
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:24,303
[man] Um… You're in the first race. Erg 9.

236
00:13:24,386 --> 00:13:27,014
-Thanks.
-Hey, there's the scout.

237
00:13:27,097 --> 00:13:30,100
I read up on him.
He was the coach at Georgetown.

238
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:32,353
Make sure you mention
you're applying to his alma mater.

239
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:34,563
Obviously.

240
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:37,316
Me too. Who isn't applying to Georgetown?

241
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:41,445
Where's your dad?
He didn't want to watch you lose?

242
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:45,950
He's overseas on business.
Had to close on a deal.

243
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:49,161
Did you hear
someone's moving to, uh, Rotterdam?

244
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,163
Where even is that?

245
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,666
Let's go, Ryder.

246
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:57,920
May the best man win.

247
00:13:58,003 --> 00:14:00,714
[intriguing music playing]

248
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:21,193
Teagan.

249
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:25,322
I know we're gonna have
to deal with this at some point,

250
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:29,201
but today I'm your coach,
and I expect you to treat me like one.

251
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:31,370
I think I get to decide.

252
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:34,248
Well, your coach has
intel on your competition,

253
00:14:34,331 --> 00:14:36,500
which will help you impress the scout.

254
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:38,252
Do you wanna hear it?

255
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:41,005
Okay, fine.

256
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:44,174
No surprise here.
Gravenhurst are likely one and two.

257
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:47,469
But there is this up-and-comer from
Claremont that you gotta watch out for.

258
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:51,765
But if you keep pace on your third 500,
you have a shot at the top spot.

259
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:52,683
Okay.

260
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:57,438
Thank you.

261
00:14:58,689 --> 00:14:59,690
You're welcome.

262
00:14:59,773 --> 00:15:01,775
This doesn't make up for smashing my mom.

263
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:05,070
Okay, well, hearing that
is punishment enough.

264
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:06,238
Mm-hmm.

265
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:09,074
About your mom…

266
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,243
Okay. No PDA.

267
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:13,996
She is home by 11, and I am up at 6.

268
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:16,707
So please,
if you're sneaking out, go earlier.

269
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:19,627
Deal.

270
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:22,588
[woman over PA]
<i>Five minutes until the U17 Men's race.</i>

271
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:31,180
Teagan?

272
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,021
Hello?

273
00:15:40,522 --> 00:15:42,024
-[David] It's just me.
-[gasps]

274
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:44,193
David.

275
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:47,738
What are you doing here?

276
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:51,367
El, I didn't mean to scare you.

277
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:55,287
I didn't think you were home,
but I just needed to get something.

278
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:58,248
Give me one good reason
why I shouldn't call the cops right now.

279
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:02,461
Because this is gonna fix everything.

280
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:04,546
[intriguing music playing]

281
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:24,566
Ryder.

282
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:28,153
You trying to mess with my Zen, faid?

283
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,282
Would that deal still be on the table
if I wanted it?

284
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:36,662
How much?

285
00:16:37,913 --> 00:16:39,164
48K.

286
00:16:40,749 --> 00:16:41,917
It's a big ask.

287
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:44,670
So is tanking my shot at junior nationals.

288
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:48,841
Yeah, I can make that happen.

289
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:50,175
[tense music playing]

290
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:52,052
You sure about it?

291
00:16:56,306 --> 00:16:57,766
You'll see in the race.

292
00:17:30,632 --> 00:17:33,510
[woman over PA] <i>All first-race rowers</i>
<i>to the floor, please.</i>

293
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:40,267
[fast-paced music playing]

294
00:17:45,814 --> 00:17:47,441
<i>♪ Nobody gonna hold me back ♪</i>

295
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:49,651
<i>♪ Nobody gonna hold me back ♪</i>

296
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:51,487
<i>♪ Nobody gonna hold me back ♪</i>

297
00:17:52,529 --> 00:17:56,366
Can I have all the rowers
from the first race, U17 Men,

298
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:58,577
on their assigned ergs, please.

299
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:01,789
<i>♪ Ain't nobody gonna hold me back ♪</i>

300
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:05,209
<i>♪ Nobody gonna hold me back</i>
<i>Nobody gonna hold me back ♪</i>

301
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:07,377
<i>♪ Nobody gonna hold me back ♪</i>

302
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:09,630
-Go!
-Let's go, Ryder.

303
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,393
-Dillinger, right?
-Yeah, that's me.

304
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:25,020
Heard you might be one to watch.

305
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:26,980
-Have a good race.
-Thank you.

306
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:30,609
[driving EDM playing]

307
00:18:33,028 --> 00:18:35,447
[woman] All competitors
are now on the floor.

308
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:39,326
<i>♪ High blood pressure, they won't catch ya</i>
<i>Tap some extra here right now ♪</i>

309
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:43,413
All rowers, pick up the handle.

310
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:48,001
Sit ready.

311
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:55,050
Attention… Go!

312
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,344
-[buzzer sounds]
-Let's go, boys!

313
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:01,598
[Teagan] Let's go, Easton!

314
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:03,433
[Hayden] Go, Easton!

315
00:19:07,771 --> 00:19:09,648
{\an8}Ryder's taking an early lead.

316
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:11,900
{\an8}[Teagan] Pull! Come on, guys!

317
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:13,986
All right. Keep it up, Easton!

318
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:20,284
{\an8}Baloo's making a move.

319
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:32,171
Baloo's pushing too hard.
He's gonna burn out.

320
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:33,881
[Teagan] He's letting Logan get to him.

321
00:19:42,097 --> 00:19:44,558
{\an8}[Hayden] Look at Josh. He's coming in hot.

322
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:54,234
[grunts]

323
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:01,200
{\an8}[Madison] Josh is losing steam.

324
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:05,537
[Hayden] Josh is dropping.

325
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:08,665
[groans]

326
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:13,003
Come on, Cam!

327
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:16,089
{\an8}[Madison] Let's go, boys! You got it!

328
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:22,429
{\an8}[Teagan] Cam's in first! Whoo!

329
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:26,683
Go, Cam!

330
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:30,896
Cam's strongest in the last 500.
It's his race to lose now.

331
00:20:32,064 --> 00:20:34,149
{\an8}[Teagan] Come on, Cam! Push!

332
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:35,901
Go, Ryder!

333
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:52,459
{\an8}[Madison] Ryder's taking over.

334
00:20:52,542 --> 00:20:55,712
{\an8}[Teagan] That doesn't make any sense.
Cam can push harder than this.

335
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:00,259
Yes! Go, Ryder!

336
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:01,551
Come on, Cam!

337
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:03,178
[Madison] Head in the game!

338
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:09,351
[Hayden] Let's go, boys! Keep it up!

339
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:20,529
{\an8}[straining]

340
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:22,030
{\an8}-[buzzer sounds]
-Yes!

341
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,199
{\an8}-Let's go!
-[crowd cheering]

342
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:27,077
Yes! Go, Ryder!

343
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:30,706
[woman] The winner
from Easton Prep, Ryder Regis.

344
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:31,957
[Hayden] Way to go!

345
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,419
-[shuddering and gasping]
-[Hayden] Way to go, team! Yes!

346
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:37,671
-Yes.
-[panting] Beat you.

347
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:39,673
Barely.

348
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:42,384
[uneasy music playing]

349
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:45,095
Hey, nice job.
You got a few minutes to chat?

350
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,222
Of course.

351
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:12,497
-Hey, what happened out there?
-I don't know what you're talking about.

352
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:16,001
Cam. Okay, you've been hitting
under a 6:20 for months.

353
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:18,545
It was yours, and then you just quit.

354
00:22:18,628 --> 00:22:19,921
Guess I choked.

355
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,882
No, not you. Not when an invite

356
00:22:21,965 --> 00:22:23,967
to the Junior National tryouts
is on the line.

357
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:25,886
That's Olympic track.

358
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:30,223
-What, did you throw the race?
-Teagan, mind your business.

359
00:22:30,724 --> 00:22:32,225
What are you doing?

360
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:34,686
A bad score will follow you
for the rest of your career.

361
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:36,438
Ryder is out talking to the scout.

362
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:38,857
-That should be you. Do you understand?
-Of course I do.

363
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:41,276
-Then why?
-Because some things are more important.

364
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,235
Like what?

365
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:45,489
[melancholy music playing]

366
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:49,284
The shop's going under
and I needed the money.

367
00:22:51,912 --> 00:22:54,289
Did someone pay you to throw the race?

368
00:22:58,585 --> 00:22:59,586
[groans]

369
00:23:01,671 --> 00:23:03,840
-It was Ryder. Oh, Cam.
-No.

370
00:23:03,924 --> 00:23:06,676
-I knew you would understand.
-There had to be a better way.

371
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:10,639
It was $48,000, Teagan. How was I
supposed to get that kind of money?

372
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:14,726
-I don't know, I…
-Then just focus on your own race.

373
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:22,567
I'm missing Teagan's competition for this.

374
00:23:24,986 --> 00:23:25,946
Explain.

375
00:23:27,030 --> 00:23:29,241
Every new hotel bled money.

376
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:33,870
My CFO stole investor funds
to pay off all the old debts.

377
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:35,330
But it wasn't just debts.

378
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:39,918
You took money for yourself,
for us, our home, our life.

379
00:23:40,001 --> 00:23:41,670
You want to know how I know?

380
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:45,715
They took everything back,
including the education fund.

381
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:46,883
El, I'm sorry.

382
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:49,886
I've been breaking my back
to keep us going.

383
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,847
I never should have been gone so long.

384
00:23:52,431 --> 00:23:56,017
My partner made it look like
it was only me, so I had to run.

385
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:59,729
I just needed time to find him
so I could fix things.

386
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:02,357
And now I can. With this.

387
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:08,447
This USB has evidence against him,
and I hid it with one of Teagan's medals.

388
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:09,614
[Ella] Are you serious?

389
00:24:10,198 --> 00:24:12,159
What happens next?

390
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:14,077
Are you gonna give that to the FBI?

391
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:16,830
No. Because it also has
evidence against me.

392
00:24:16,913 --> 00:24:18,999
-[Ella sighs]
-My deal's with my partner,

393
00:24:19,082 --> 00:24:22,294
and he's willing to pay me
a lot of money for this USB.

394
00:24:22,377 --> 00:24:24,754
How does this fix anything?

395
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:26,756
It'll set you and Teagan up.

396
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:31,011
-You can use the money to go back to LA.
-I don't want to leave, David.

397
00:24:31,595 --> 00:24:32,846
Teagan and I…

398
00:24:34,639 --> 00:24:35,932
We've built a life here.

399
00:24:39,686 --> 00:24:40,687
What are you gonna do?

400
00:24:40,770 --> 00:24:45,025
If I turn myself in,
I could go to jail for 20 years.

401
00:24:45,108 --> 00:24:47,152
I can't do that, Ella.

402
00:24:51,781 --> 00:24:52,908
[door opens]

403
00:24:52,991 --> 00:24:57,037
[footsteps approaching]

404
00:25:01,124 --> 00:25:02,792
Keep running then.

405
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:06,129
I wanna see Teagan.

406
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:08,340
You don't get to see Teagan.

407
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:14,304
Not until you make things right,
and this is not making things right.

408
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:26,858
-Your heat's in ten.
-Thank you.

409
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:32,989
Hey, Madison, uh, I need a favor.

410
00:25:33,073 --> 00:25:36,618
Our parents might be bedfellows,
but I don't think we're there just yet.

411
00:25:36,701 --> 00:25:39,162
It's for Cam, and you can't ask why.

412
00:25:39,246 --> 00:25:41,665
Just know I wouldn't be asking
if it wasn't important.

413
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:45,460
You saw what happened with him.

414
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:48,213
Okay, what can I do?

415
00:25:50,549 --> 00:25:52,676
I need you
to put me on the same erg as Cam.

416
00:25:53,593 --> 00:25:55,595
[intriguing music playing]

417
00:25:56,972 --> 00:25:57,973
Okay.

418
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:05,230
[woman] Next race, U17 Women.

419
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,801
All rowers, pick up the handle.

420
00:26:35,385 --> 00:26:38,096
-Did Teagan switch ergs?
-I'm not keeping track.

421
00:26:38,179 --> 00:26:39,681
[woman] Sit ready.

422
00:26:39,764 --> 00:26:42,559
-Attention… Go!
-[buzzer sounds]

423
00:26:42,642 --> 00:26:44,686
["Muscle" by METTE playing]

424
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:49,608
<i>♪ What's underneath is real, I'm sure ♪</i>

425
00:26:49,691 --> 00:26:51,943
<i>♪ What you've got's impressive ♪</i>

426
00:26:52,027 --> 00:26:54,696
<i>♪ It caught my attention ♪</i>

427
00:26:54,779 --> 00:26:58,033
Looking good, Teag.
You got this! You got this!

428
00:26:58,116 --> 00:27:01,494
<i>♪ Don't waste my time</i>
<i>'Cause time ain't free ♪</i>

429
00:27:01,578 --> 00:27:05,040
<i>♪ Just cross the line and step to me ♪</i>

430
00:27:05,123 --> 00:27:07,208
<i>♪ Pump it up</i>
<i>Electric ♪</i>

431
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:10,295
<i>♪ Make the cut</i>
<i>'Cause I get what I want ♪</i>

432
00:27:11,546 --> 00:27:12,631
She's dropping.

433
00:27:12,714 --> 00:27:14,841
Come on, Teagan. You're faster than this.

434
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:16,968
Maybe she's just having an off day?

435
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:18,762
[Cam] Come on!

436
00:27:20,972 --> 00:27:22,515
[Madison] You got it!

437
00:27:25,644 --> 00:27:26,519
[grunts]

438
00:27:26,603 --> 00:27:28,480
She's working hard,
but running out of time.

439
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:30,982
[Cam] What is she up to?

440
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:39,032
-[buzzer sounds]
-[woman] The winner is Lara Robinson.

441
00:27:39,532 --> 00:27:40,492
[grunts]

442
00:27:43,828 --> 00:27:45,955
Twelfth. She's not gonna like that.

443
00:27:49,834 --> 00:27:51,044
Uh…

444
00:27:51,127 --> 00:27:53,046
There's, uh, something wrong with my erg.

445
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:54,923
What's she doing?

446
00:27:58,468 --> 00:27:59,803
[woman] You called me over?

447
00:28:10,105 --> 00:28:11,231
What happened out there?

448
00:28:11,731 --> 00:28:15,777
There was something wrong with my erg.
It probably affected your race as well.

449
00:28:16,736 --> 00:28:17,904
Teagan, what did you do?

450
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,072
[quiet, tense music playing]

451
00:28:19,155 --> 00:28:20,156
Nothing.

452
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:27,163
Okay, well, Teagan, you were right.

453
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:29,833
The judges determined there was
an obstruction on the drivetrain,

454
00:28:29,916 --> 00:28:32,544
so they're gonna take the erg
out of the rest of the races.

455
00:28:32,627 --> 00:28:34,629
-What about our scores?
-You can't race again today.

456
00:28:34,713 --> 00:28:35,880
You wouldn't have the energy.

457
00:28:35,964 --> 00:28:38,633
So they've agreed
to strike your scores from the record.

458
00:28:39,759 --> 00:28:40,719
I'm sorry, guys.

459
00:28:40,802 --> 00:28:42,929
I know how much
you wanted to impress this scout,

460
00:28:43,012 --> 00:28:44,180
but it is what it is.

461
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:46,516
They will set up a time for you to re-row.

462
00:28:46,599 --> 00:28:48,810
That's gonna be set
by the president of the jury, okay?

463
00:28:48,893 --> 00:28:49,978
-Okay.
-[Hayden] Okay?

464
00:28:50,061 --> 00:28:51,062
Thank you.

465
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:54,649
[woman] No. It's sticking.

466
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,318
We're gonna have to replace
the whole thing.

467
00:29:02,198 --> 00:29:03,658
What the hell, Teagan?

468
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:06,161
-Okay.
-Look, you shouldn't have done that.

469
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:08,538
You were about to throw away
everything you worked for, Cam.

470
00:29:08,621 --> 00:29:11,875
Yeah, but that was my choice.
You threw away your chance with the scout.

471
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:14,961
-Yeah, well, that was mine.
-Look, I told you to stay out of this.

472
00:29:15,044 --> 00:29:17,881
You were the one who said there are
more important things than rowing,

473
00:29:17,964 --> 00:29:22,135
and you know what? You are right.
You. You are more important.

474
00:29:33,104 --> 00:29:34,981
You need to stay out of my mess.

475
00:29:35,648 --> 00:29:40,153
[melancholy music playing]

476
00:29:43,114 --> 00:29:44,240
-[phone buzzing]
-[sighs]

477
00:29:44,324 --> 00:29:45,241
[beeps]

478
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:46,910
Hey.

479
00:29:46,993 --> 00:29:47,994
[Hayden] <i>Hey.</i>

480
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:50,872
So I've got some good news
and some bad news.

481
00:29:50,955 --> 00:29:53,041
Bad news is Teagan's race
got scratched today,

482
00:29:53,124 --> 00:29:55,251
but she will get a chance to re-race.

483
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:57,629
And the good news?

484
00:29:57,712 --> 00:30:01,090
The good news is she is open to us dating.

485
00:30:01,591 --> 00:30:05,053
Ish. With some minor restrictions.

486
00:30:06,221 --> 00:30:07,680
About that, um…

487
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:11,935
I think we need to put things on hold.

488
00:30:12,852 --> 00:30:13,728
Oh.

489
00:30:14,687 --> 00:30:15,730
Uh…

490
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:20,151
Is-is-is everything okay?
Did I do something?

491
00:30:20,235 --> 00:30:22,779
No, it's definitely not you.

492
00:30:23,738 --> 00:30:25,782
<i>I just need to be alone right now.</i>

493
00:30:27,742 --> 00:30:28,743
Okay.

494
00:30:30,495 --> 00:30:33,790
<i>If that's what you want,</i>
<i>that's what you need, um…</i>

495
00:30:35,124 --> 00:30:36,835
I guess, take care of yourself, El.

496
00:30:50,139 --> 00:30:52,809
[Logan] Nice job, man. I saw you in there,
you looked pretty good.

497
00:30:53,309 --> 00:30:54,894
Thanks, you were looking good too.

498
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:56,104
-[Logan] It went well.
-Hey!

499
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:57,230
Right on.

500
00:30:57,772 --> 00:31:01,442
Watch this one.
He's cute, enjoys late night chats.

501
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:04,821
-And stabbing you in the back.
-Excuse me. What is your problem?

502
00:31:04,904 --> 00:31:06,531
Don't pretend, it's insulting.

503
00:31:07,365 --> 00:31:10,201
-You ghosted me.
-Because you sabotaged us at the regatta.

504
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:11,327
What?

505
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:14,163
You asked me to hook up in the boathouse.
And when I left you,

506
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:17,542
you cut Josh's oar
so it would snap during the race.

507
00:31:17,625 --> 00:31:19,836
Girl, do you know
how crazy you sound right now?

508
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:21,504
Don't play dumb. I know it was you.

509
00:31:25,925 --> 00:31:27,594
You know, I replayed that day.

510
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:30,346
Over and over again in my head.

511
00:31:30,430 --> 00:31:33,850
I'm trying to understand
why you blocked me.

512
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:39,022
Hey, what changed? What would make
this incredible guy start to hate me?

513
00:31:40,023 --> 00:31:42,358
Turns out, you believed
I was capable of the worst things.

514
00:31:43,026 --> 00:31:44,027
Good to know, I guess.

515
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:45,695
But…

516
00:31:47,113 --> 00:31:48,156
It had to be you.

517
00:31:48,656 --> 00:31:51,451
You were alone in there, and you were
the only one who could've done it.

518
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:52,911
You wanted to leave first.

519
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:56,873
You asked me to wait five minutes
before I left, so I did.

520
00:31:56,956 --> 00:31:58,541
And I wasn't even alone in there.

521
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:00,877
-[suspenseful music playing]
-What do you mean?

522
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:04,255
As I was leaving, I heard
somebody coming through the window.

523
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:06,257
They didn't see me, but…

524
00:32:06,758 --> 00:32:07,967
I saw them.

525
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:13,181
It was your stroke. Josh.

526
00:32:20,897 --> 00:32:21,898
You!

527
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:25,318
-You goddamn liar, you lied to my face.
-Whoa, Loo.

528
00:32:25,401 --> 00:32:27,654
-I don't know what you're talking about.
-The oar.

529
00:32:28,237 --> 00:32:29,113
You did it.

530
00:32:29,197 --> 00:32:31,074
And you let Logan take the fall for it.

531
00:32:32,575 --> 00:32:34,035
Look, it's not what you think.

532
00:32:34,661 --> 00:32:39,040
You watched me break up with him.
You psychopath!

533
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:41,125
I wanted to tell you.

534
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:44,087
-But you didn't.
-Hold on, Baloo. What's going on?

535
00:32:44,170 --> 00:32:45,004
Baloo, come on.

536
00:32:45,088 --> 00:32:46,464
You know what you did.

537
00:32:46,547 --> 00:32:51,094
And soon, everyone else will know
you sabotaged the race.

538
00:32:51,177 --> 00:32:52,512
[tense music playing]

539
00:32:52,595 --> 00:32:54,222
What is he talking about?

540
00:32:54,305 --> 00:32:56,015
-None of your business.
-Josh.

541
00:32:56,099 --> 00:32:58,059
Teagan, get away from my car.

542
00:32:58,142 --> 00:33:00,979
No. Not until you tell me what's going on.

543
00:33:06,818 --> 00:33:07,819
Fine.

544
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:09,862
[engine roaring]

545
00:33:09,946 --> 00:33:12,532
-[Teagan] What was Baloo talking about?
-[Josh] Just leave it alone.

546
00:33:12,615 --> 00:33:13,783
Did you cut the oar?

547
00:33:13,866 --> 00:33:16,869
Oh my God.
Why is everyone always on my case?

548
00:33:16,953 --> 00:33:19,539
Just answer me! Did you or didn't you?

549
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:22,291
Everybody wants a piece of me.

550
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:26,671
And then why does everybody
need me to do something that I can't do?

551
00:33:26,754 --> 00:33:28,464
Hey, hey, Josh…

552
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:31,801
No, nothing is ever enough!

553
00:33:34,679 --> 00:33:37,557
-I don't think you're okay. We should…
-No, I'm fine, okay? I'm…

554
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:41,352
-[stammering] I have to be fine. I…
-Josh.

555
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:42,812
[Josh grunts in pain]

556
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:44,897
-Josh?
-[groans]

557
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:46,858
-[tires screech]
-[screams]

558
00:33:51,821 --> 00:33:52,989
[Teagan groans]

559
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:56,200
[panting]

560
00:33:56,743 --> 00:34:00,580
Oh my gosh! Josh! Josh, Josh!
Hey! Hey, hey, hey!

561
00:34:00,663 --> 00:34:01,956
-Whoa. Hey.
-You're okay.

562
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:05,043
-You blacked out. We went off the road.
-What's going on?

563
00:34:05,126 --> 00:34:06,502
-But I just…
-What?

564
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:09,589
-I don't think you're okay. I'll call 911.
-Teagan, your head.

565
00:34:09,672 --> 00:34:11,716
-You're gonna go to the hospital.
-What?

566
00:34:11,799 --> 00:34:13,634
-No. Wait!
-Stay here. Okay? Hold on.

567
00:34:13,718 --> 00:34:15,219
-No…
-We're gotta call someone.

568
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:17,346
-What if you black out again?
-Wait one sec!

569
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:19,682
That's why we can't call anyone.

570
00:34:21,684 --> 00:34:23,811
-[Josh] Oh shit.
-Okay.

571
00:34:23,895 --> 00:34:26,105
-Oh, shit, this is really bad.
-[Teagan] This is serious.

572
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:28,608
We've gotta call someone. I'm gonna…

573
00:34:29,275 --> 00:34:30,359
Wait! No. No, no, no!

574
00:34:30,443 --> 00:34:33,071
-What are you doing?
-I'm thinking, okay?

575
00:34:33,154 --> 00:34:34,489
What is there to think about?

576
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:39,744
[grunting in pain]

577
00:34:40,661 --> 00:34:43,039
[gasping and shuddering]

578
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:45,124
You're sick, aren't you?

579
00:34:47,376 --> 00:34:52,215
The pills that you took at your party,
is that part of it? And then the sabotage?

580
00:34:52,298 --> 00:34:53,883
[Josh, crying] Yeah, I am.

581
00:34:54,383 --> 00:34:55,426
[sniffles]

582
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:00,973
I have a heart condition.

583
00:35:03,351 --> 00:35:04,727
It's getting worse.

584
00:35:07,063 --> 00:35:08,064
Well…

585
00:35:08,564 --> 00:35:11,067
Are you gonna have a heart attack?
Do your parents know?

586
00:35:11,150 --> 00:35:15,530
No, I can't tell them.
Everything's a competition.

587
00:35:16,030 --> 00:35:17,657
They can't…

588
00:35:18,741 --> 00:35:21,619
-They can't know that their son's…
-What?

589
00:35:21,702 --> 00:35:23,204
[Josh panting]

590
00:35:23,287 --> 00:35:24,664
Hey, what?

591
00:35:27,041 --> 00:35:28,292
Defective.

592
00:35:29,335 --> 00:35:30,336
They won't think that.

593
00:35:30,920 --> 00:35:33,005
They only love me if I win.

594
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:38,219
When you fail in my family,
the sun just stops shining on you.

595
00:35:38,803 --> 00:35:41,681
When Ryder got stroke seat,
he got my internship.

596
00:35:41,764 --> 00:35:44,767
And now he's going to be
making the junior national team,

597
00:35:44,851 --> 00:35:46,936
and I'm next to my messed up car!

598
00:35:47,019 --> 00:35:48,980
I can't hide this.

599
00:35:53,609 --> 00:35:56,737
I know, I know it's dysfunctional, I just…

600
00:35:58,656 --> 00:36:00,575
I still don't want to let down my dad.

601
00:36:01,075 --> 00:36:03,161
[somber music playing]

602
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:05,538
You have to see a doctor
and tell your parents

603
00:36:05,621 --> 00:36:07,456
before you seriously hurt yourself.

604
00:36:07,540 --> 00:36:09,417
I know. It's just…

605
00:36:11,669 --> 00:36:14,046
Easton's hosting the Haverford Cup.

606
00:36:14,130 --> 00:36:15,882
My granddad's gonna be there,

607
00:36:15,965 --> 00:36:17,967
and all of his buddies
are gonna be watching, and…

608
00:36:21,220 --> 00:36:24,348
I wanna show my family my best
before I tell them.

609
00:36:24,432 --> 00:36:27,518
Give me one last regatta
before I walk away.

610
00:36:29,061 --> 00:36:32,732
Okay, I know how to buy you some time.
But you have to see a doctor.

611
00:36:35,401 --> 00:36:36,402
Okay.

612
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:41,908
I know someone who can fix this.

613
00:36:44,911 --> 00:36:46,579
[vehicle approaching]

614
00:37:11,687 --> 00:37:13,189
I need a favor.

615
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:21,781
[intriguing music playing]

616
00:38:16,752 --> 00:38:18,754
[music ends]
